cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ast-guard in your research, please cite it using this file."
type: software
title: "ast-guard: Pre-Execution Structural Gate for AI-Generated Code"
version: 2.3.0
date-released: 2026-06-27
url: "https://github.com/Nick-is-building/ast-guard"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "Nick"
    alias: "Nick-is-building"
abstract: >
  ast-guard is a deterministic, model-free AST-based detector for structural
  reward hacking in RL-trained code models. It evaluates LLM-generated code
  against eight structural checks (hardcoding, complexity collapse, forbidden
  calls, import drift, extensional enumeration, behavioral risk, literal hijack,
  and new constant bypass) before any code runs. Empirically validated in a
  GRPO training loop (Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct, 150 steps), where it reduced
  structural hack rate from ~99% to ~0% under a λ=2.0 penalty. Companion
  experiment: github.com/Nick-is-building/rl-rewardhacking (extends
  ariahw/rl-rewardhacking).
keywords:
  - reward hacking
  - RL safety
  - code generation
  - static analysis
  - AST
  - structural detection
  - GRPO
references:
  - type: software
    title: "rl-rewardhacking: Steering RL Training Interventions to Mitigate Reward Hacking"
    url: "https://github.com/Nick-is-building/rl-rewardhacking"
    notes: "Companion experiment repo. Extends ariahw/rl-rewardhacking with ast-guard as a live structural penalty."
  - type: software
    title: "rl-rewardhacking (upstream)"
    authors:
      - name: "ariahw"
    url: "https://github.com/ariahw/rl-rewardhacking"
    notes: "Upstream repo: 'Steering RL: Training Interventions to Mitigate Reward Hacking'"
